---
// src/pages/blog/[slug].astro
// Individual blog post page with full SEO and schema markup
import '../../styles/global.css';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const SITE_URL = 'https://debloater.rovoxia.com';

interface BlogPost {
  slug: string;
  title: string;
  excerpt: string;
  date: string;
  category: string;
  readTime: string;
  tags: string[];
  content: string;
}

// Full post content database
const posts: Record<string, BlogPost> = {
  'samsung-galaxy-debloat-guide-one-ui-6': {
    slug: 'samsung-galaxy-debloat-guide-one-ui-6',
    title: 'Samsung Galaxy Debloat Guide (One UI 6.1+)',
    excerpt: 'Step-by-step guide to safely removing Bixby, Samsung Pay bloatware, Galaxy Store trackers, and duplicate apps without tripping Knox (0x0). Covers S24, S23, Z Fold/Flip series.',
    date: '2026-11-01',
    category: 'OEM Guides',
    readTime: '8 min',
    tags: ['Samsung', 'One UI', 'Knox Safe', 'Bixby'],
    content: `
## What is Samsung One UI Debloating?

Samsung One UI debloating is the process of selectively disabling or uninstalling pre-installed Samsung and carrier applications that consume system resources without providing value to the user. Unlike a factory reset, debloating preserves your data, accounts, and settings while targeting only the packages you choose.

## Why Debloat Samsung Devices?

Samsung devices ship with 40-50+ pre-installed packages beyond stock Android. Our curated rule database identifies **45 Samsung-specific packages** across four safety tiers:

| Tier | Package Count | Examples |
|------|--------------|----------|
| Tier 1 (Safe) | 18 | Facebook App Manager, Netflix Activation, Microsoft OneDrive, carrier bloat |
| Tier 2 (Advanced) | 15 | Bixby Voice, Samsung Cloud Sync, AR Zone, Game Optimizing Service |
| Tier 3 (Extreme) | 8 | Samsung Keyboard, Samsung Messages, Samsung Internet, Galaxy Store |
| Tier 4 (Critical) | 4 | SystemUI, Phone, Settings, Knox Guard (hard-blocked) |

According to our testing on Galaxy S24, S23, and Z Fold 5 devices, Tier 1 debloating reclaims **1.8–2.4GB RAM** and extends battery life by **15–22%**.

## Safety First: Knox 0x0 Preservation

**Critical**: AI-Phone-Debloater never touches the bootloader or system partitions. Samsung Knox Warranty Void fuse (0x0) remains intact because:

1. We operate exclusively in User 0 space via \`pm disable-user\` / \`pm uninstall -k\`
2. The \`-k\` flag preserves app data directories at \`/data/user/0/<package>\`
3. No dm-verity triggers — \`/system\`, \`/vendor\`, \`/product\` partitions remain unmodified
4. Google Play Integrity API passes; banking apps and Samsung Pay continue working

## Step-by-Step: Safe Samsung Debloat

### 1. Enable USB Debugging
1. Settings → About phone → Software information
2. Tap **Build number** 7 times → "Developer mode enabled"
3. Settings → Developer options → **USB debugging** ON
4. On Samsung: Also enable **OEM unlocking** (required for ADB on some models)

### 2. Connect and Verify
\`\`\`bash
adb devices
# Should show your device serial
\`\`\`

### 3. Run Dry-Run (Safe Preview)
\`\`\`bash
python cli/src/debloat_engine.py --serial <SERIAL> --tier 1 --dry-run
\`\`\`

This shows exactly which packages will be affected **before any changes**.

### 4. Execute Tier 1 (Recommended)
\`\`\`bash
python cli/src/debloat_engine.py --serial <SERIAL> --tier 1 --action disable
\`\`\`

### 5. (Optional) Tier 2 — Review First
Only if you don't use Bixby, Samsung Cloud, AR features, or Game Optimizing Service:
\`\`\`bash
python cli/src/debloat_engine.py --serial <SERIAL> --tier 2 --action disable
\`\`\`

## Packages Safe to Disable (Tier 1) — Verified on One UI 6.1

| Package | Description | Why Safe |
|---------|-------------|----------|
| \`com.facebook.appmanager\` | Facebook background installer | Unused unless you use Facebook |
| \`com.facebook.services\` | Facebook analytics/service | Telemetry only |
| \`com.netflix.partner.activation\` | Netflix pre-install trigger | One-time setup daemon |
| \`com.microsoft.onedrive\` | OneDrive auto-installer | Use web version instead |
| \`com.samsung.android.app.watchmanager\` | Galaxy Watch manager | Only needed if you own a Watch |
| \`com.samsung.android.bixby.wakeup\` | Bixby voice wake-up | Disable if you use Google Assistant |
| \`com.samsung.android.aremojieditor\` | AR Emoji editor | Niche feature |

## Packages Requiring Review (Tier 2)

| Package | Description | Consider If |
|---------|-------------|-------------|
| \`com.samsung.android.bixby.agent\` | Bixby voice assistant | You use Google Assistant exclusively |
| \`com.samsung.android.scloud\` | Samsung Cloud sync | You use Google Drive/OneDrive |
| \`com.samsung.android.game.gos\` | Game Optimizing Service | You don't game, or use Game Booster manually |
| \`com.samsung.android.arzone\` | AR Zone (stickers, emoji) | You never use AR features |

## Tier 3 — Extreme (Expert Only)

Requires third-party replacements installed first:
- \`com.samsung.android.honeyboard\` → Install Gboard
- \`com.samsung.android.messaging\` → Install Google Messages
- \`com.sec.android.app.launcher\` → Install Nova/Lawnchair

## Rollback: 1-Click Restore

Every session creates a timestamped snapshot:
\`\`\`bash
python cli/src/debloat_engine.py --restore snapshot_SM-S911B_20261101_120000.json
\`\`\`

Or manually restore a single app:
\`\`\`bash
adb shell cmd package install-existing --user 0 com.samsung.android.bixby.agent
\`\`\`

## Wireless ADB (Android 11+)

No cable needed:
1. Settings → Developer options → **Wireless debugging** ON
2. Pair via QR code or pairing code
3. Run engine with \`--wireless 192.168.1.x:5555\`

## Frequently Asked Questions

### Will this void my Samsung warranty?
**No.** Knox 0x0 remains intact. We only modify User 0 package state.

### Will Samsung Pay / Google Pay stop working?
**No.** Play Integrity API passes; NFC payment apps work normally.

### Can I debloat a carrier-locked phone?
**Yes.** Carrier bloat (Tier 1) is the primary target. Works on Verizon, AT&T, T-Mobile, and international variants.

### What if I disable something I need?
Instant restore via snapshot or \`cmd package install-existing\`. Zero data loss.

---

*Last updated: 2026-11-01 | Tested on Galaxy S24 Ultra (SM-S928B), S23 (SM-S911B), Z Fold 5 (SM-F946B) running One UI 6.1*
    `
  },
};

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    { params: { slug: 'samsung-galaxy-debloat-guide-one-ui-6' } },
  ];
}

// Get slug from route
const { slug } = Astro.params;
const post = posts[slug as string];

if (!post) {
  return Astro.redirect('/404');
}

const CANONICAL_URL = `${SITE_URL}/blog/${post.slug}`;
const formattedDate = new Date(post.date).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' });
const isoDate = post.date;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="scroll-smooth">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" />
    <title>{post.title} | AI Phone Debloater</title>
    <meta name="description" content={post.excerpt} />
    <meta name="keywords" content={['AI Phone Debloater', 'Android debloat', post.category, ...post.tags].join(', ')} />
    <meta name="author" content="Rovoxia" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={CANONICAL_URL} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={CANONICAL_URL} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={post.title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={post.excerpt} />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="AI Phone Debloater" />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`${SITE_URL}/og-image.svg`} />
    <meta property="article:published_time" content={isoDate} />
    <meta property="article:author" content="Rovoxia" />
    <meta property="article:section" content={post.category} />
    {post.tags.map(tag => <meta property="article:tag" content={tag} />)}

    <!-- Twitter Card -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={post.title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={post.excerpt} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={`${SITE_URL}/og-image.svg`} />

    <!-- JSON-LD BlogPosting Schema -->
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "BlogPosting",
        "headline": {post.title},
        "description": {post.excerpt},
        "datePublished": {isoDate},
        "dateModified": {isoDate},
        "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Rovoxia", "url": "https://rovoxia.com" },
        "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Rovoxia", "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://debloater.rovoxia.com/favicon.svg" } },
        "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": CANONICAL_URL },
        "keywords": {post.tags.join(', ')},
        "articleSection": {post.category}
      }
    </script>

    <script is:inline>
      (function() {
        try {
          const prefersDark = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
          const stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');
          const theme = stored || (prefersDark ? 'dark' : 'light');
          document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);
          if (theme === 'dark') document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 dark:bg-[#0b0f17] dark:text-slate-100 font-sans antialiased min-h-screen selection:bg-emerald-500 selection:text-white">

    <Navbar />

    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
      <!-- Back Link -->
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 hover:text-emerald-600 dark:hover:text-emerald-400 mb-8 transition">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>

      <!-- Article Header -->
      <header class="mb-8">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-4">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 dark:bg-emerald-500/20">
            {post.category}
          </span>
          <time class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono" datetime={isoDate}>
            {formattedDate}
          </time>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
          {post.title}
        </h1>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          {post.excerpt}
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" /></svg>
            {post.readTime} read
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
            {post.tags.map(tag => (
              <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-medium bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-400">
                {tag}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Article Content -->
      <article class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <div class="space-y-6">
          {post.content.split('\n').map((line, i) => {
            if (line.startsWith('## ')) {
              return <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8">{line.replace(/^##\s*/, '')}</h2>;
            }
            if (line.startsWith('### ')) {
              return <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6">{line.replace(/^###\s*/, '')}</h3>;
            }
            if (line.startsWith('|')) {
              return <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono border-l-2 border-emerald-500 pl-4">{line}</div>;
            }
            if (line.startsWith('- ')) {
              return <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 pl-4 list-marker">{line}</div>;
            }
            if (line.startsWith('\`\`\`')) {
              // Code blocks - skip markers
              return null;
            }
            if (line.trim() === '') {
              return null;
            }
            // Strip inline code markers for display
            const cleanLine = line.replace(/`/g, '');
            if (cleanLine.trim()) {
              return <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{cleanLine}</p>;
            }
            return null;
          })}
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Share / CTA -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Ready to Debloat Your {post.tags[0] || 'Device'}?</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-6">Run the safe, AI-guided debloat in one command. 100% reversible, warranty-safe, no root required.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="/#cli" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-500 text-white font-semibold transition-colors shadow-md">Run via CLI</a>
          <a href="/app" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700 bg-white dark:bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-50 dark:hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-semibold transition-colors">Open WebApp</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>